IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `kn-nouns`
IMPORT `kn-ch1`
IMPORT `kn-majority`
IMPORT `kn-majority-fixed`

-- Mishnah Kinnim: CLAIMS A SOLVER SHOULD REFUTE.  Every #ASSERT here is a statement some reading or
-- some intuition makes about every way the birds could have gone, and that is false: `l4 prove` should
-- answer each with a counterexample, which the evaluator replays.  ./prove.sh treats "refuted" as the
-- expected verdict for this file, and anything else (proved, unknown) as a failure.  A refutation is
-- what shows the bounds in kn-obligations.l4 are the least ones, and that the harness can say no.
-- Not checked by ../check.sh, for the same reason as kn-obligations.l4.

§ `Kinnim: claims that fail`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a whole number from 0 to` n x MEANS x AT LEAST 0 AND x AT MOST n AND (FLOOR x) EQUALS x

§§ `Before the fact: two burnt offerings from 1-2-3-10-100 are safe (1:3 says one)`

ASSUME X1 IS A NUMBER
ASSUME X2 IS A NUMBER
ASSUME X3 IS A NUMBER
ASSUME X4 IS A NUMBER
ASSUME X5 IS A NUMBER

#ASSERT (`a whole number from 0 to` 2 X1 AND `a whole number from 0 to` 4 X2 AND `a whole number from 0 to` 6 X3 AND `a whole number from 0 to` 20 X4 AND `a whole number from 0 to` 200 X5 AND X1 PLUS X2 PLUS X3 PLUS X4 PLUS X5 EQUALS 2) IMPLIES (X1 AT MOST 1 AND X2 AT MOST 2 AND X3 AT MOST 3 AND X4 AT MOST 10 AND X5 AT MOST 100)

§§ `After the fact: 201 of the Mishnah's 232 are certainly valid (the least is 200)`

ASSUME A1 IS A NUMBER
ASSUME A2 IS A NUMBER
ASSUME A3 IS A NUMBER
ASSUME A4 IS A NUMBER
ASSUME A5 IS A NUMBER

#ASSERT (`so many of a nest's birds could be above` 1 A1 AND `so many of a nest's birds could be above` 2 A2 AND `so many of a nest's birds could be above` 3 A3 AND `so many of a nest's birds could be above` 10 A4 AND `so many of a nest's birds could be above` 100 A5 AND A1 PLUS A2 PLUS A3 PLUS A4 PLUS A5 EQUALS 116) IMPLIES ((`the valid offerings of a nest of pairs with so many of its birds above` 1 A1) PLUS (`the valid offerings of a nest of pairs with so many of its birds above` 2 A2) PLUS (`the valid offerings of a nest of pairs with so many of its birds above` 3 A3) PLUS (`the valid offerings of a nest of pairs with so many of its birds above` 10 A4) PLUS (`the valid offerings of a nest of pairs with so many of its birds above` 100 A5) AT LEAST 201)

§§ `Tiferet Yisrael's rule on R. Heller's 1-2-3-4-5: ten of each kind, twenty birds (the least is 16)`

ASSUME H1 IS A NUMBER
ASSUME H2 IS A NUMBER
ASSUME H3 IS A NUMBER
ASSUME H4 IS A NUMBER
ASSUME H5 IS A NUMBER

#ASSERT (`so many of a nest's birds could be above` 1 H1 AND `so many of a nest's birds could be above` 2 H2 AND `so many of a nest's birds could be above` 3 H3 AND `so many of a nest's birds could be above` 4 H4 AND `so many of a nest's birds could be above` 5 H5 AND H1 PLUS H2 PLUS H3 PLUS H4 PLUS H5 EQUALS 15) IMPLIES ((`the valid offerings of a nest of pairs with so many of its birds above` 1 H1) PLUS (`the valid offerings of a nest of pairs with so many of its birds above` 2 H2) PLUS (`the valid offerings of a nest of pairs with so many of its birds above` 3 H3) PLUS (`the valid offerings of a nest of pairs with so many of its birds above` 4 H4) PLUS (`the valid offerings of a nest of pairs with so many of its birds above` 5 H5) AT LEAST 20)

§§ `Filling both containers, on Gewirtz's 3-3-3-5-5: 22 birds (the least is 20)`

ASSUME G1 IS A NUMBER
ASSUME G2 IS A NUMBER
ASSUME G3 IS A NUMBER
ASSUME G4 IS A NUMBER
ASSUME G5 IS A NUMBER

#ASSERT (`so many of a nest's birds could be above` 3 G1 AND `so many of a nest's birds could be above` 3 G2 AND `so many of a nest's birds could be above` 3 G3 AND `so many of a nest's birds could be above` 5 G4 AND `so many of a nest's birds could be above` 5 G5 AND G1 PLUS G2 PLUS G3 PLUS G4 PLUS G5 EQUALS 19) IMPLIES ((`the valid offerings of a nest of pairs with so many of its birds above` 3 G1) PLUS (`the valid offerings of a nest of pairs with so many of its birds above` 3 G2) PLUS (`the valid offerings of a nest of pairs with so many of its birds above` 3 G3) PLUS (`the valid offerings of a nest of pairs with so many of its birds above` 5 G4) PLUS (`the valid offerings of a nest of pairs with so many of its birds above` 5 G5) AT LEAST 22)

-- The control for section F of kn-obligations.l4: the same equation is false for an obligation that
-- owes one burnt offering more than it owes sin offerings, even for whole numbers of pairs and of birds
-- above within the nest; so the solver is not passing section F for nothing.
ASSUME P IS A NUMBER
ASSUME U IS A NUMBER

#ASSERT (((FLOOR P) EQUALS P) AND (`so many of a nest's birds could be above` P U)) IMPLIES (`the valid offerings of an obligation with so many of its birds above` (`Unassigned obligation` WITH `sin offerings owed` IS P, `burnt offerings owed` IS P PLUS 1) U EQUALS `the valid offerings of a nest of pairs with so many of its birds above` P U)

-- The control for kn-fixed-arity.l4: for five owners with any counts, one valid offering more than
-- twice the smallest majority is not assured, so the solver is not passing the bound for nothing.
ASSUME Q51 IS A NUMBER
ASSUME Q52 IS A NUMBER
ASSUME Q53 IS A NUMBER
ASSUME Q54 IS A NUMBER
ASSUME Q55 IS A NUMBER
ASSUME B51 IS A NUMBER
ASSUME B52 IS A NUMBER
ASSUME B53 IS A NUMBER
ASSUME B54 IS A NUMBER
ASSUME B55 IS A NUMBER

#ASSERT ((((FLOOR Q51) EQUALS Q51) AND (Q51 AT LEAST 1)) AND (((FLOOR Q52) EQUALS Q52) AND (Q52 AT LEAST 1)) AND (((FLOOR Q53) EQUALS Q53) AND (Q53 AT LEAST 1)) AND (((FLOOR Q54) EQUALS Q54) AND (Q54 AT LEAST 1)) AND (((FLOOR Q55) EQUALS Q55) AND (Q55 AT LEAST 1)) AND (`so many of a nest's birds could be above` Q51 B51) AND (`so many of a nest's birds could be above` Q52 B52) AND (`so many of a nest's birds could be above` Q53 B53) AND (`so many of a nest's birds could be above` Q54 B54) AND (`so many of a nest's birds could be above` Q55 B55) AND ((B51 PLUS B52 PLUS B53 PLUS B54 PLUS B55) EQUALS (Q51 PLUS Q52 PLUS Q53 PLUS Q54 PLUS Q55))) IMPLIES (((`the valid offerings of a nest of pairs with so many of its birds above` Q51 B51) PLUS (`the valid offerings of a nest of pairs with so many of its birds above` Q52 B52) PLUS (`the valid offerings of a nest of pairs with so many of its birds above` Q53 B53) PLUS (`the valid offerings of a nest of pairs with so many of its birds above` Q54 B54) PLUS (`the valid offerings of a nest of pairs with so many of its birds above` Q55 B55)) AT LEAST ((2 TIMES (`the smallest majority of five nests` Q51 Q52 Q53 Q54 Q55)) PLUS 1))
